@scene(500)

// Stand-ins anywhere. A shape's stand-in, name.simple, is the simpler model
// the viewer draws once the shape is small on screen, below the Detail
// slider's Simple rung. It is measured at the point, as feature pruning is,
// so a long part simplifies its far end first; and it may sit on any value,
// so a screw placed through a remap keeps the stand-in its library gave it.
// Raise the Simple rung and zoom out, or look along the bar.
//
// Its size is name.featureSize where declared, else the value's box. A
// fastener carries the smallest extent of its declared box with its stand-in,
// which is how a screw read through map.patternRectangularXY, whose box no
// analysis can follow, still knows when to switch.

// A field of M6 cap screws on a 25 mm grid, cropped to the plate: each screw
// is placed by a remap, and each draws its socket near and its plain head and
// shank far.
plate = box([-100.0, -100.0, -12.0], [100.0, 100.0, 0.0]);
plate.color = [0.40, 0.44, 0.50];
screws = max(remap(fastener.shcs(6.0, 20.0), map.patternRectangularXY([25.0, 25.0])),
             abs(p.x) - 95.0, abs(p.y) - 95.0);

// A bar 400 mm long with a groove 2 wide and 1.5 deep across its top and
// bottom every 20 mm; its stand-in is the plain bar. Seen along its length,
// the near grooves stay and the far ones go.
groove = max(abs(((p.x % 20.0) + 20.0) % 20.0 - 10.0) - 1.0, 8.5 - abs(p.z));
bar = max(box([-200.0, 140.0, -10.0], [200.0, 160.0, 10.0]), neg(groove));
bar.simple = box([-200.0, 140.0, -10.0], [200.0, 160.0, 10.0]);
bar.color = [0.70, 0.62, 0.45];

return plate, screws, bar;
